WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.000
Having a rival can keep you committed to achieving your goals and enhance your overall performance.
有一个竞争对手，能让你始终致力于实现自己的目标，并提升你的整体表现。

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:15.780
But before you go out and find an entrepreneur to outcompete, it’s important to understand and avoid the traps that often come with rivalry.
但在你出去物色一位创业者、想要在竞争中胜过对方之前，重要的是先了解并避开与对手较量时常常随之而来的陷阱。

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:27.040
After all, competitive rivalry can also hinder effective decision-making and increase your willingness to take risks, behaviors that can ultimately hurt your venture’s success.
毕竟，与对手较量也可能妨碍你做出有效的决策，并让你更愿意冒险，而这些行为最终可能有损你企业的成功。

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:35.140
Finding someone you’re committed to outcompeting can be a great way to stay focused on your goals and push your venture to the next level.
找到一个你决心在竞争中胜过的人，会是一个很好的办法，能让你始终专注于目标，把企业推向新的高度。

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:45.730
But when you’re intently focused on outperforming your rivals, you may begin to develop a “win-at-all-costs” mentality that causes you to ignore how you achieve success.
但是，一旦你一心专注于胜过对手，就可能开始形成一种“不惜一切代价求胜”的心态，导致你忽视自己用什么方式取得成功。

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:53.010
One group of researchers, for example, examined the link between rivalry and unethical behavior.
例如，有一组研究人员考察了对手间的较量与不道德行为之间的关联。

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:59.580
They found that when people compete against their rivals, they are more willing to behave unethically to win.
他们发现，人们与对手竞争时，更愿意为了取胜而做出不道德的行为。

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:05.820
But such behavior may stain your reputation and strain relationships important to your success.
但这类行为可能会玷污你的声誉，并使那些对你的成功很重要的关系变得紧张。

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:10.730
One way to avoid this trap is to stop and reflect on what’s important.
避开这一陷阱的一个方法是停下来，反思什么才是重要的。

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:18.830
While outperforming your rivals may provide short-term benefits, the loss of your integrity will have long-term consequences.
虽然胜过对手或许能带来短期利益，但失去诚信将会造成长期后果。

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:27.260
One reason having a rival can enhance your venture’s performance is that it creates a level of excitement that drives you to work harder.
有竞争对手能提升你企业的业绩，原因之一在于它会带来一定程度的兴奋感，驱使你更加努力地工作。

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:36.220
But this eagerness to win may also hurt your venture’s success, particularly when it causes you to make impulsive, irrational decisions.
但这种急于求胜的心情也可能有损你企业的成功，尤其是在它导致你做出冲动、不理性的决定时。

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:53.480
But it’s possible to avoid such costly mistakes by making a habit of engaging in critical thinking, such as considering opposing viewpoints and conducting cost-benefit analyses, especially for those decisions that are complex and can determine the future of your venture.
但这类代价高昂的错误是可以避免的，办法是养成批判性思考的习惯，比如考虑对立的观点、开展成本效益分析，尤其是在面对那些复杂且能决定你企业未来的决策时。

00:01:54.280 --> 00:02:03.880
The sense of eagerness that comes with having a rival can not only cause you to make poorer decisions but also lead you to take greater risks that put your venture in peril.
有了竞争对手，随之而来的急切感不仅可能让你做出更糟糕的决定，还可能促使你冒更大的风险，使你的企业陷入危险。

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:17.970
One way you can overcome the risk-inducing effects of rivalry that stand to endanger your venture’s success is to remain attentive to your emotional state and actively monitor how such feelings are affecting your decision-making.
与对手较量会诱发冒险倾向，这种影响很可能危及你企业的成功；要克服它，一个办法是始终留意自己的情绪状态，并主动监测这些情绪正如何影响你的决策。
